#!/bin/sh
# Keep the fpt skill in step with the CLI. The command reference under skills/fpt/ is generated
# from the command docstrings; this regenerates it when the CLI changes and stops the commit so
# the result can be reviewed and staged. CI fails on stale docs either way.
#
# Enable once per clone:  git config core.hooksPath .githooks
set -e
if git diff --cached --name-only | grep -qE '^(src/fpt/|scripts/skill_docs\.py|skills/fpt/|parity/dimensions\.toml)'; then
    if ! uv run --quiet python -m scripts.skill_docs --check >/dev/null 2>&1; then
        uv run --quiet python -m scripts.skill_docs
        echo "pre-commit: the skill docs were stale and have been regenerated." >&2
        echo "Review them, 'git add skills/fpt', and commit again." >&2
        exit 1
    fi
fi
